<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius von Pflug</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1499–1564</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius von Pflug was a German humanist and Catholic theologian who sought reconciliation with the Lutherans and helped draft the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> Interim of 1548. Elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg">Naumburg</a> in 1541, he was kept out by the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-of-amsdorf">Nicholas of Amsdorf</a> until 1547. As the last Catholic bishop of Naumburg, his death in 1564 left the see to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> administrators.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-von-pflug.jpg" alt="Julius von Pflug" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Julius_von_Pflug_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
